0.930 0.960 1.000 rg
46.00 709.89 503.28 33.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.130 0.360 0.680 rg 54.00 731.39 Td (Easy Answer \(In Simple Words\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.150 0.200 rg 54.00 719.89 Td (We used the official benchmark split \(~85% Training = 125,973 rows, ~15% Testing = 22,544) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.150 0.200 rg 54.00 709.39 Td (rows\), where the test set includes 17 unseen zero-day attack types.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 698.89 Td (ï Why We Used the Official Split Instead of a Random 80/20 Split:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 687.39 Td (A random train_test_split puts the exact same attack types in both train and test, giving an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 676.59 Td (unrealistic 99.5% score. The official KDDTest+ split holds out 17 novel attack types ONLY in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 665.79 Td (the test set!) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 652.49 Td (ï Validation Split During Deep Neural Network Training:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 640.99 Td (Inside the 125,973 training records, our Deep Neural Network reserves an additional 15%) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 630.19 Td (validation split \(validation_split=0.15\) for EarlyStopping and learning-rate tuning.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 616.89 Td (ï Strict Zero Data-Leakage Policy:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 605.39 Td (Our MinMaxScaler and LabelEncoders are fit\(\) strictly on KDDTrain+ and only transform\(\) is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 594.59 Td (called on KDDTest+, ensuring zero test information leaks into training.) Tj ET
