BT /F2 10.5 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 46.00 516.39 Td (Q8.  Are there any ethical / privacy issues with your dataset?) Tj ET
0.930 0.980 0.950 rg
46.00 467.89 503.28 33.00 re f
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.110 0.480 0.260 rg 54.00 489.39 Td (Easy Answer \(In Simple Words\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.150 0.200 rg 54.00 477.89 Td (The dataset is completely anonymized \(no real personal IPs, names, or payload text\), and we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.150 0.200 rg 54.00 467.39 Td (added strict ethical guardrails for automated IP blocking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 456.89 Td (ï 1. Complete User Privacy \(No PII or Packet Payloads\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 445.39 Td (NSL-KDD contains only statistical flow metadata \(byte counts, durations, flags\). It does NOT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 434.59 Td (contain private user emails, passwords, web URLs, or personally identifiable IP addresses.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 421.29 Td (ï 2. Ethical Risk of False Positives in Automated Blocking:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 409.79 Td (In real-world cybersecurity, if an AI falsely flags a normal user \(False Positive\) and auto-) Tj ET
