BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 689.39 Td (NSL-KDD reflects classic TCP/IP attacks \(like Telnet, FTP, and Smurf DoS\) and lacks modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 678.59 Td (cloud-native attacks, API exploits, or encrypted HTTPS/QUIC malware traffic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.7 Tf 0.100 0.130 0.180 rg 48.00 665.29 Td (ï 2. Severe Scarcity of U2R & R2L Samples:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 653.79 Td (With only 52 U2R \(User-to-Root\) samples out of 125,973 training rows, supervised models) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.220 0.260 0.320 rg 58.00 642.99 Td (struggle to learn every possible privilege-escalation variation without heuristic help.) Tj ET
